& [Fold1IdentityAndPurpose] distinguishes the adapter
  + the provider-neutral contract names the existing pure runtime operations in one closed request union and one closed response form
  + the MCP adapter exposes exactly one stateless tool named coordinate_attention
  + the purpose is a model-host seam between inference passes rather than a model provider a scheduler or another semantic authority
  + existing cantor-shared-attention JSON behavior remains compatible while sharing the same execution function

& [Fold2ActorsAuthorityAndBoundary] keeps tool use subordinate
  + a host or model proposes a complete request but cannot invent a valid participant generation policy digest evidence or attestation by naming the tool
  + cantor_core remains the sole transition authority and returns typed success backpressure or refusal
  + the MCP adapter only bounds parses delegates serializes and labels the result
  + registration with Codex Ollama llama.cpp or another host is an operator-owned later step
  + no call performs model inference network access persistence effect execution signing or hidden-state mutation

& [Fold3DataAndSchema] makes the seam machine-discoverable
  + SharedAttentionToolRequest is a deny-unknown-fields tagged union over validate_frame reconcile compact prepare settle fork_dream validate_dream record_dream_evidence review_dream discard_dream and project_dream_promotion
  + SharedAttentionToolResult is a closed typed union covering every operation result without erasing domain structure
  + SharedAttentionToolResponse contains profile operation status optional typed result optional typed fault and mandatory nonclaims
  + JsonSchema derives from the same Rust forms used for strict deserialization
  + the MCP tool wraps exactly one request property and publishes closed input and output schemas

& [Fold4ExecutionAndTransport] closes one call
  + the host serializes one complete request and invokes coordinate_attention
  + the adapter rejects absent malformed unknown or oversized arguments before core execution
  + the core executes exactly one pure transition or validation and returns one response
  + MCP structuredContent is the complete authoritative machine response while text content is only a bounded summary
  + succeeded and buffered responses are MCP successes; refused invalid-request and internal-fault responses set the MCP error flag while preserving structuredContent
  + stdio is the only server transport in P0 and the server retains no frame between calls

& [Fold5AttentionAndReentry] preserves the intended inference loop
  + a host may place the returned successor frame into a later inference prompt or tool call
  + exact generation and digest binding prevents a later pass from silently updating stale state
  + buffered status instructs the host to compact split or defer rather than overfill the declared attention account
  + settlement identifies a stable semantic checkpoint for the next pass but is not external truth
  + DreamFrame remains hypothetical until reviewed promotion re-enters ordinary reconciliation

& [Fold6HonestySecurityAndProof] prevents adapter laundering
  + generated schema and runtime deserializer must reject unknown fields and unknown operation names
  + direct core execution CLI execution direct MCP execution and official MCP client execution must agree on structured response bytes for the same canonical request
  + semantic refusal must never become transport success without its refused status and error flag
  + buffered backpressure must remain a successful typed disposition and never mutate the supplied frame
  + tool annotations declare read-only non-destructive idempotent and closed-world behavior
  + server instructions repeat no hidden state no effects no truth-by-settlement and no invented bindings

& [Fold7PruningGrowthAndPhaseLock] selects one small adapter
  + retain shared request and response forms pure dispatch one MCP crate one stdio binary schemas and tests
  + prune model invocation host registration sessions durable frame storage network listeners transport authentication streaming subscriptions concurrency coordination and deployment
  + reuse rmcp schemars serde and the completed shared-attention core
  + do not widen route_attention query_sop or their existing authority identities
  + later work may add a digest-addressed session service or provider loop around this stateless seam under new authority
  + [exhaustion_state] is seven_fold_phase_locked_for_stateless_adapter_P0

& [Flowchart] is executable
  + A0 host holds one exact frame or dream artifact
  + A1 host or model emits one closed SharedAttentionToolRequest
  + A2 adapter bounds and parses the request
  + A3 core validates and executes one pure operation
  + A4 adapter returns one complete structured response
  + A5 host reflects on the response in a later inference pass
  + A6 host re-enters with the returned exact successor or stops on refusal backpressure or terminal settlement

& [DualHemisphereReview] reconciles accessibility and control
  + holistic side gains one compact callable handle for the full semantic frame lifecycle
  + delineating side keeps state explicit calls atomic adapters stateless schemas closed and authority in the core
  + reconciliation permits repeated creative inference passes without implying live shared neural state

& [ResidualFrontier] remains visible
  + full frames can be context-expensive and a later content-addressed store may replace repeated payload transport
